# Captured drives and their derived caches. Around 40 GB lives here and none of it was
# ignored, so a stray `git add -A` would have staged the lot -- the same staging hazard the
# LFS rules in CLAUDE.md exist for, minus the smudge error to warn you.
#
# Scoped here rather than in the root .gitignore on purpose: that file is upstream's and
# every fork-only entry in it is another conflict at the next sync.
#
# The analysis scripts beside this file stay tracked; only the data they read does not.
device_data/
device_data_speedmax/
device_routes/
drive_logs/
sla_drive_logs/
test_data/
lkas_block_c4/
backup_params/
rlogs_validation/

# derived from the above, all regenerable
.lkas_block_cache/
*.zst
*.csv
tune_metrics_cache.jsonl
lkas_block_scenarios.json
lkas_block_pr_data.json
accel_cmd_characterization.json

# plots: *.png is LFS-tracked against a push-inaccessible remote, so committing one bricks
# device installs (CLAUDE.md). Regenerate from the tool that drew it instead.
*.png
*.svg
